KG42.register("nodes-209796eed73259b11b5b7d1a",{"id":"COMP-a88f30097237f433","code":"SET039","label":"Uniform electricity-price settlement linked to aggregate consumption","definition":"A user's per-period payment is its own consumption quantity multiplied by the uniform price determined by total consumption: \\mathrm{payment}_n^k=x_n^k p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal N}x_m^k), where the total quantity includes user n's own consumption.","layer":"L8","template_code":"QSC","concept_id":"settlement.payment","concept_ids":["settlement.payment"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: the user's time-period electricity charge","Operation: this user's consumption quantity multiplied by the total-quantity price that includes its own consumption","Output: individual payment amount under a given consumption allocation"]},"exclusions":["Applicable to the single-price game for price anticipators","The price function p_k and the consumption allocation vary by time period","The consumption vector is selected by the user within its feasible set"],"members":[{"id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","market_meaning":"Each user's slot payment equals its own slot consumption multiplied by p_k evaluated at the aggregate consumption of all users in that slot. Scope: Each user's per-slot payment in the price-anticipating single-price game. Condition: Given the users' consumption profile.","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Each user's per-slot payment in the price-anticipating single-price game.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25"]},"constraint_refs":["36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"4b90ba4bff73d096e1a1b80026731ec732edba3ed979a8f018672423aef88700","paper":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","rule_ref":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009","node_id":"settlement.payment","function":"settlement.payment","unit_id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-a-M03::settlement.payment","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["36-dsm_mechanism_design"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-0fb1d9d41e-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"1174","section":"II-D-2 Price Anticipating Users","anchor_text":"for resource allocation. Given , the energy A. provider sets a single price for time slot . User the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We consider the following pricing scheme for resource allocation. Given \\mathbf{x}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N), the energy provider sets a single price \\mu_k(\\mathbf{x})=p_k(\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_n^k) for time slot k. User n then pays x_n^k p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k) for that time slot.","paper":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"We consider the following pricing scheme for resource allocation. Given \\mathbf{x}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N), the energy provider sets a single price \\mu_k(\\mathbf{x})=p_k(\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_n^k) for time slot k. User n then pays x_n^k p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k) for that time slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-0fb1d9d41e-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"1174","section":"II-D-2 Price Anticipating Users","anchor_text":"for resource allocation. Given , the energy A. provider sets a single price for time slot . User the","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We use the notation \\mathbf{x}_{-n} to denote the vector of all consumption powers chosen by users other than user n, i.e., \\mathbf{x}_{-n}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_{n-1},\\mathbf{x}_{n+1},\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N). Then, given \\mathbf{x}_{-n}, the payoff of each user n is obtained as Q_n(\\mathbf{x}_n;\\mathbf{x}_{-n}) = U_n\\left(\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}} x_n^k\\right) - \\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}} x_n^k p_k\\left(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k\\right). \\tag{13} The payoff function Q_n is similar to P_n, defined for price-taking users in (11). The only difference is that while the payoff function P_n takes the price \\lambda_k as a fixed parameter, price anticipating users realize that the price is set according to p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k), and adjust their payoffs accordingly.","paper":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","quote":"We use the notation \\mathbf{x}_{-n} to denote the vector of all consumption powers chosen by users other than user n, i.e., \\mathbf{x}_{-n}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_{n-1},\\mathbf{x}_{n+1},\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N). Then, given \\mathbf{x}_{-n}, the payoff of each user n is obtained as Q_n(\\mathbf{x}_n;\\mathbf{x}_{-n}) = U_n\\left(\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}} x_n^k\\right) - \\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}} x_n^k p_k\\left(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k\\right). \\tag{13} The payoff function Q_n is similar to P_n, defined for price-taking users in (11). The only difference is that while the payoff function P_n takes the price \\lambda_k as a fixed parameter, price anticipating users realize that the price is set according to p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k), and adjust their payoffs accordingly."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["aggregate_demand_price_consumption_payment"],"projection_statuses":["clear"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L8-642d510f9a","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L8","ontological_kind":"aggregate_demand_price_consumption_payment"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-a-M03::settlement.payment","paper_id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","function":"settlement.payment","source_occurrences":[{"id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R009","market_meaning":"Each user's slot payment equals its own slot consumption multiplied by p_k evaluated at the aggregate consumption of all users in that slot. Scope: Each user's per-slot payment in the price-anticipating single-price game. Condition: Given the users' consumption profile.","omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Each user's per-slot payment in the price-anticipating single-price game.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25"]},"constraint_refs":["36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"4b90ba4bff73d096e1a1b80026731ec732edba3ed979a8f018672423aef88700"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Each user's slot payment equals its own slot consumption multiplied by p_k evaluated at the aggregate consumption of all users in that slot. Scope: Each user's per-slot payment in the price-anticipating single-price game. Condition: Given the users' consumption profile.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25"],"ref":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-0fb1d9d41e-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"1174","section":"II-D-2 Price Anticipating Users","anchor_text":"for resource allocation. Given , the energy A. provider sets a single price for time slot . User the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We consider the following pricing scheme for resource allocation. Given \\mathbf{x}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N), the energy provider sets a single price \\mu_k(\\mathbf{x})=p_k(\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_n^k) for time slot k. User n then pays x_n^k p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k) for that time slot."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"For each user n and each time slot k, the user's payment for that slot is its own slot consumption x_n^k multiplied by the single price p_k evaluated at the sum of all users' slot consumptions.","expression":"\\mathrm{payment}_n^k = x_n^k \\, p_k\\!\\left(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k\\right), \\quad n\\in\\mathcal{N}.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x-n-k"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-p-k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26"],"ref":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E25","location":{"location_id":"src-0fb1d9d41e-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":"1174","section":"II-D-2 Price Anticipating Users","anchor_text":"for resource allocation. Given , the energy A. provider sets a single price for time slot . User the","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"We consider the following pricing scheme for resource allocation. Given \\mathbf{x}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N), the energy provider sets a single price \\mu_k(\\mathbf{x})=p_k(\\sum_{n\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_n^k) for time slot k. User n then pays x_n^k p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k) for that time slot."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E26","location":{"location_id":"src-0fb1d9d41e-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"1174","section":"II-D-2 Price Anticipating Users","anchor_text":"for resource allocation. Given , the energy A. provider sets a single price for time slot . User the","equation_id":"(13)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"We use the notation \\mathbf{x}_{-n} to denote the vector of all consumption powers chosen by users other than user n, i.e., \\mathbf{x}_{-n}=(\\mathbf{x}_1,\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_{n-1},\\mathbf{x}_{n+1},\\ldots,\\mathbf{x}_N). Then, given \\mathbf{x}_{-n}, the payoff of each user n is obtained as Q_n(\\mathbf{x}_n;\\mathbf{x}_{-n}) = U_n\\left(\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}} x_n^k\\right) - \\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal{K}} x_n^k p_k\\left(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k\\right). \\tag{13} The payoff function Q_n is similar to P_n, defined for price-taking users in (11). The only difference is that while the payoff function P_n takes the price \\lambda_k as a fixed parameter, price anticipating users realize that the price is set according to p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal{N}} x_m^k), and adjust their payoffs accordingly."}]}],"variables":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x-n-k","symbol":"x_n^k","meaning":"Power consumption level of user n in time slot k; the k-th component of the consumption vector x_n selected by user n in the price-anticipating game.","kind":"operational","domain":"x_n^k is the k-th component of a vector x_n ∈ X_n, where X_n is user n's feasible energy-consumption set; the exact per-slot bounds are not stated in the supplied E25 quotation.","unit":null,"indices":["n","k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E27"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","declaration_ref":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::x::v141-c-R009-x-n-k"}],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-p-k","symbol":"p_k","meaning":"Single-price schedule function for time slot k, evaluated at aggregate slot consumption; the provider sets μ_k(x)=p_k(∑_{n∈N} x_n^k).","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"p_k(\\cdot)"},"unit":null,"indices":["k"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E25","v141-b-g01-E26"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R009","declaration_ref":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::theta::v141-c-R009-p-k"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-a-M03::settlement.payment","stage":"L8","subtype":"aggregate_demand_price_consumption_payment","projection_status":"clear","target_definition":"A user's per-period payment is its own consumption quantity multiplied by the uniform price determined by total consumption: \\mathrm{payment}_n^k=x_n^k p_k(\\sum_{m\\in\\mathcal N}x_m^k), where the total quantity includes user n's own consumption.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: the user's time-period electricity charge","Operation: this user's consumption quantity multiplied by the total-quantity price that includes its own consumption","Output: individual payment amount under a given consumption allocation"],"variation_fields":["Applicable to the single-price game for price anticipators","The price function p_k and the consumption allocation vary by time period","The consumption vector is selected by the user within its feasible set"],"constraint_refs":["36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C001","36-dsm_mechanism_design::v141-c-R009::v141-c-R009-C002"],"paper_id":"36-dsm_mechanism_design","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","function":"settlement.payment","template_code":"QSC"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/202"});
